    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "03363b4f_83256956",
        "filename": "rust/config/global.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1208973
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-01T17:20:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe it does affect debugging.  Although testing locally, even with this flag gdb can find the sources if I\u0027m in the same directory as them, so it\u0027s not simply just checking the absolute path.\n\nMatthew, what do you think is the best way of handling this?",
      "parentUuid": "af5ed17d_f2e21d42",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "917ceeea8085fa674a2abd89d4ea52b79671e5a2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "32486232_50780a8d",
        "filename": "rust/config/global.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-01T17:45:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The primary advantage of having a source tree key in a binary is that you can more cleanly use gdb\u0027s set substitute-path feature if you have a binary containing things from two separate source trees.\n\nFor example, if you build an out-of-tree binary which linked against something from the platform, but wanted to be able to debug through it, you could do\n\nset substitute-path /android/ /path/to/my/android\nset substitute-path /some-other-proj/ /path/to/the/other/proj\n\n(or even place such in your .gdbinit)\nwhich would allow you to correctly resolve source from multiple trees.\n\nThat said, if we are already using a relative path for C++, we\u0027ve already lost this ability, so it might be best to just follow the relative path.\n\ntl;dr:\nUsing a leading /tree-name/ is more composable.\nIf we are already using a relative path in C++, we\u0027ve already lost this composability, and it\u0027d be fine to just do the same thing C++ does, this isn\u0027t a rust-specific decision.",
      "parentUuid": "03363b4f_83256956",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "917ceeea8085fa674a2abd89d4ea52b79671e5a2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
